From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:16:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: fit the bin pointers of all layers of a tiler
 context in one heap chunk

A layered pass at a large framebuffer size loses the device: kbase logs
"Queue group to be terminated, couldn't handle the OoM event". vkd3d-proton
hits it with every pass that has no RTV or DSV: it sets renderArea to
maxFramebufferWidth x maxFramebufferHeight and layerCount to
maxFramebufferLayers (65536 x 65536 x 256 here), so 20 of its 2.14.1 tests
(draw_uav_only, null_rtv, the atomic tests, ...) time out. Upstream PanVK
does the same.

On the device (G615, drawcpu noatt: zero attachments, five 3-vertex draws
with fragment atomics) it fails from 3 layers at 4096x4096 and from 8
layers at 4096x4096 down to 2048x2048 passing; 1 and 2 layers pass at any
size, up to 65536x65536. Raising the heap maximum from 400 to 4096 chunks
doesn't help (the group is terminated after 1 s instead of 0.1 s), and 8
chunks are enough for 2 layers. With PANVK_DEBUG=trace the heap top moves
down by DIV_ROUND_UP(bins, 8) * 8 * 16 bytes per layer of the tiler
context, for every layer at once (349,568 bytes per layer at 4096x4096,
mask 0x1fe). Three layers need 1,048,704 bytes, more than a 1 MiB chunk
minus its 64-byte header holds, so every chunk the OOM handler links is too
small as well, until the heap reaches its maximum.

The hierarchy mask budget was the whole chunk per tiler context, counted
at 8 bytes per bin, which keeps one layer under half a chunk but not three.
Count 16 bytes per bin on v10+ and divide the chunk between the layers of a
tiler context (up to MAX_LAYERS_PER_TILER_DESC = 8 on v10/v11). Passes with
one or two layers get the same mask as before; larger layered passes drop
their finest bin levels until the layers fit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: GPU hang fix: layered passes (3+ layers at ~3.6k px and up) lost the device with a tiler heap OOM kbase can't recover from (no incremental rendering on uAPI 1.21): the v10+ tiler takes 16 bytes per bin (counted as 8) and the bin pointers of all layers of a tiler context from one 1 MiB chunk; count 16 B/bin and split the chunk budget between the layers. vkd3d-proton hits it with every pass without RTV/DSV (renderArea = max framebuffer size, 256 layers)
Upstream-commit: none
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: applies after rg477m/042; pan_desc.c change also applies to gallium panfrost v10/v11 (only when the budget is the limit)
Validation test: native repro (drawcpu noatt: no attachments, fragment atomics, 5 draws): device lost from 3 layers at 4096x4096 on rg477m/042, all 12 points of 1/2/3/8/256 layers x 2048..65536 px PASS (500/500) with no kbase OoM; PanProbe 38/38; ircheck colour/depth checksums identical; combined build noatt2.so (98a13fc24329, rg477m/001-044): vkd3d-proton 2.14.1 full suite 289 -> 306 PASS vs rg477m/042 (17 of the 20 B19 timeouts pass, the 2 ROV tests now fail instead of hanging, 1 stream-output test still times out; test_integer_blending_pipeline_state's start-up crash is B20: 6/20 on both builds), suite time 50 -> 13 min; DXVK unchanged: Hades renders, Jupiter Hell tutorial 48.5 fps, Serious Sam D3D11 58.3 fps (FPS limiter off, quietd Stock)
Channel: compatibility, unsafe
Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/lib/pan_desc.c                 |  7 ++++++-
 src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_desc.c b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_desc.c
index d213c304..70ca15f5 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_desc.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_desc.c
@@ -1729,7 +1729,12 @@ static uint32_t
 pan_calc_bins_pointer_size(uint32_t width, uint32_t height, uint32_t tile_size,
                            uint32_t hierarchy_mask)
 {
-   const uint32_t bin_ptr_size = PAN_ARCH >= 12 ? 16 : 8;
+   /* The CSF tilers (v10+) take 16 bytes per enabled bin from the heap: on
+    * a G615 (v11) the heap top of a 4096x4096 pass with mask 0x1fe (21845
+    * bins) moves down by DIV_ROUND_UP(21845, 8) * 8 * 16 bytes per layer.
+    * v10 is assumed to match; overestimating only drops fine levels sooner.
+    */
+   const uint32_t bin_ptr_size = PAN_ARCH >= 10 ? 16 : 8;
 
    uint32_t bins_x[PAN_BIN_LEVEL_COUNT];
    uint32_t bins_y[PAN_BIN_LEVEL_COUNT];
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
index 39da551b..fa500adc 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
@@ -1541,9 +1541,18 @@ get_tiler_desc(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf)
       ASSERTED unsigned max_levels = tiler_features.max_levels;
       assert(max_levels >= 2);
 
-      /* The tiler chunk start with a header of 64 bytes */
+      /* The tiler chunk start with a header of 64 bytes. The tiler takes
+       * the bin pointers of all the layers of a tiler context from one heap
+       * chunk at once: if they don't fit, every new chunk the OOM handler
+       * links is too small as well, until the heap reaches its maximum and
+       * the queue group is terminated. Split the budget between the layers
+       * of a tiler context. */
+      const uint32_t td_layers =
+         CLAMP(cmdbuf->state.gfx.render.layer_count, 1,
+               MAX_LAYERS_PER_TILER_DESC);
       cfg.hierarchy_mask = panvk_select_tiler_hierarchy_mask(
-         phys_dev, &cmdbuf->state.gfx, phys_dev->csf.tiler.chunk_size - 64);
+         phys_dev, &cmdbuf->state.gfx,
+         (phys_dev->csf.tiler.chunk_size - 64) / td_layers);
       cfg.fb_width = fb->width_px;
       cfg.fb_height = fb->height_px;
 
